> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

> REVIEW: Missing main ingredient added without invented amount: cooked chicken

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @crumbled gorgonzola cheese{1/16%cup}, @gluten-free elbow macaroni{2%oz}, @butter{3/4%tbsp}, @shredded Monterey Jack cheese{1/4%cup}, @gluten-free 1:1 baking flour{3/4%tbsp}, @hot sauce (such as Frank's Redhot){1/16%cup} (or more to taste), @ground black pepper{1/8%pinch}, @milk{3/8%cup}, @shredded Cheddar cheese{1/4%cup}, @cooked chicken{}.

== Preparation ==

Cook gluten-free macaroni according to its package. Make a butter and gluten-free flour roux, whisk in milk and cook until thickened. Melt in the cheeses, stir in hot sauce and fold in pasta and fully cooked chicken. Chicken amount is missing and must be decided before cooking.
